Subject: [202605] Preserve groff build data in sonic-slave containers

post_run_cleanup deletes /usr/share/groff, including the PostScript DESC
file and macro definitions required to compile Bash documentation on Trixie.
Keep those tool inputs in build containers; retain runtime image cleanup.
The failing build reached binary-doc but could not generate bash.pdf.

Verified source: 8076a44fa579fde75f73299f03e7f3cac298d9e3.
Failure: https://github.com/ITJamie/sonic-vs-builder/actions/runs/42528445500
Remove when upstream cleanup preserves build-time groff inputs.

--- a/src/sonic-build-hooks/scripts/post_run_cleanup
+++ b/src/sonic-build-hooks/scripts/post_run_cleanup
@@ -46,9 +46,14 @@
 while [ -n "$(find /usr/share/doc -depth -type d -empty -print -exec rmdir {} +)" ]; do :; done && \
     rm -rf               \
     /usr/share/man/*     \
-    /usr/share/groff/*   \
     /usr/share/info/*    \
     /usr/share/lintian/* \
     /usr/share/linda/*   \
     /var/cache/man/*     \
     /usr/share/locale/*
+
+# groff device descriptions/macros are compiler inputs, not disposable docs.
+# Packages such as Bash generate documentation inside sonic-slave containers.
+if [[ ! ${IMAGENAME} =~ -slave- ]]; then
+    rm -rf /usr/share/groff/*
+fi
